  "description": "VUVKOO crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C160 H220 Gd10 N10 O50,3(C2 H3 N1),8(C1 H1 Cl3),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1P (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2P (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3P (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4P (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5P (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd9 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd10 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1Q (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2Q (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3Q (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4Q (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5Q (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd16 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd17 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd18 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd19 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd20 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.830-3.865 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.34-114.44°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C176H240Cl24Gd10N14O53.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
